@startuml
title ADR-001 - On-Demand Architecture and Authority Boundaries
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
left to right direction

actor User
cloud "Microsoft OneDrive\nMicrosoft Graph" as Graph
component "Existing synchronisation engine\n(remote + local processing)" as Sync
database "Item database\nAUTHORITATIVE FUSE NAMESPACE\nremote metadata + stable hydration state" as DB
component "FUSE presentation / access layer" as Fuse
rectangle "User-visible sync_dir\n~/OneDrive" as View
folder "Physical sync_dir beneath mount\nHYDRATED CONTENT ONLY" as Disk
component "Existing local change detection\ninotify + reconciliation" as Local

User --> View : browse / open / edit
View --> Fuse
Fuse --> DB : namespace / metadata /\nhydration state
Fuse --> Disk : hydrated content I/O
Fuse --> Sync : hydration request\nwhen content required

Graph <--> Sync : existing Graph / delta processing
Sync --> DB : authoritative namespace updates
Sync --> Disk : existing validated download path
Sync --> DB : commit stable hydration state\nafter storage transition
Disk --> Local : events for resident content
Local --> Sync : existing local change path
Sync --> Graph : existing upload / delete / rename

note right of DB
FUSE presents what the database says
belongs in the eligible namespace.
No physical placeholder is required.
end note

note bottom of Disk
Physical storage answers whether
content is resident and supplies
local-change evidence.
end note

note bottom of Fuse
FUSE does not become a second
Microsoft Graph sync engine.
end note
@enduml
